#### Technical Details

[`getClaimable()`](https://github.com/3jane-protocol/moneymarket-contracts/blob/bcfbebfac56f0e8d1497efde6524eeb3e4d553ea/src/jane/RewardsDistributor.sol#L198) returns the user’s uncapped delta `totalAllocation - claimed[user]` but ignores the global cap based on `maxClaimable - totalClaimed`. The cap is only enforced during [`_claim()`](https://github.com/3jane-protocol/moneymarket-contracts/blob/bcfbebfac56f0e8d1497efde6524eeb3e4d553ea/src/jane/RewardsDistributor.sol#L169), where the amount is reduced to the remaining global cap.

#### Impact

Informational.

#### Recommendation

Change `getClaimable()` to apply the cap:

```solidity
function getClaimable(address user, uint256 totalAllocation) external view returns (uint256) {
    if (maxClaimable == 0 || totalClaimed >= maxClaimable) return 0;

    uint256 alreadyClaimed = claimed[user];
    uint256 uncapped = totalAllocation > alreadyClaimed ? totalAllocation - alreadyClaimed : 0;

    uint256 remaining = maxClaimable - totalClaimed;
    return uncapped > remaining ? remaining : uncapped;
}
```

#### Developer Response

Acknowledged.
